WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:04.313
This project combines join reasoning with a
window-function idea from the previous

00:00:04.339 --> 00:00:09.948
module Inside the common table expression LEAD looks
forward within

00:00:09.974 --> 00:00:14.451
each patient's admissions ordered by admit date That
gives us the next

00:00:14.477 --> 00:00:19.865
department and next admission date The outer query
keeps rows where a

00:00:19.878 --> 00:00:24.881
next department exists and where the department
actually changes Then it groups

00:00:24.907 --> 00:00:30.026
from-department and to-department to summarize
transition counts and average days between
admissions

00:00:31.847 --> 00:00:37.110
Run the query and inspect the transitions that
appear Even though the

00:00:37.123 --> 00:00:41.228
final step is not a traditional join the same grain
thinking applies

00:00:42.165 --> 00:00:46.060
The sequence CTE has one row per admission with
information about the

00:00:46.073 --> 00:00:50.599
following admission The grouped result then changes
the grain to one row

00:00:50.625 --> 00:00:56.207
per department transition pair When combining
advanced SQL techniques

00:00:56.431 --> 00:00:58.865
keep stating the grain after every major step
